course: dictionary
lesson: 4317
title: Group: a set, a band, or to put together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. As a noun, group means a number of things or people that are together or belong together, like «a group of friends».
explain: «A charity is a group that helps people or animals; to donate is to give money to help.» Here group means people working together, and the clue is helps people or animals. The word to donate tells you what the charity does.
explain: Group can also be a verb. To group things is to put them into sets, as in «group the shapes by colour». Try your meaning in the sentence: if «put the shapes into sets by colour» still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Group means a number of things or people that are together or belong together.
fact: A group can also be a band that plays music.
fact: As a verb, «group» means to put things together in sets, like «group the shapes by colour».
fact: «4 groups of 3» means 4 × 3, and «put into 2 equal groups» means divide by 2.
fact: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost: its mother may be fishing nearby, so keep away and call a rescue group.»
exercise: «In 2026 the 48 teams were split into 12 groups of 4.» What does groups mean here? | Games played alone | Money given to help | *Sets of teams put together | Bands that play music
exercise: Mia says group only means a band of musicians. What is the best reply? | *No, it can also mean a set of people or things | Yes, that is the only meaning | Yes, and it also means a dog | No, it means to give money
exercise: «Group the shapes by colour.» What is the verb group doing here? | *Putting the shapes into sets | Painting the shapes | Counting the shapes | Throwing the shapes away
test: «Each group played 6 games, and there were 12 groups.» How many games did each group play? | *6 | 72 | 4 | 12
test: «A charity is a group that helps people or animals.» What does group mean in this sentence? | A band that plays music | *A set of people working together | A number of games | To put things into sets
exam: «Put 8 cubes into 2 equal groups.» Which sum shows this? | 8 + 2 | *8 ÷ 2 | 8 − 2 | 8 × 2
